<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:20Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>How two directors fought back when their film was stolen — and won an International Emmy Award</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c882fc7dda1c4399fa64a7f549fb1e41d9d9b4a416cbdda2c9b833fc03972921</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-two-directors-fought-back-when-their-film-was-stolen-and-won-an-international-emmy-award/a-76103455--47858310f097.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-two-directors-fought-back-when-their-film-was-stolen-and-won-an-international-emmy-award/a-76103455?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two German film students confronted the American who won festival prizes with their animated movie. "The Talented Mr. F," their documentary on their fight against plagiarism, is now in the spotlight.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Istanbul 'lion hunt' ends with no big cat found after all</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e380209cb8ee4d7b1482bb4897b8b96f6a332673fef23839798ae70ca838a4d3</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/istanbul-lion-hunt-ends-with-no-big-cat-found-after-all/a-80020913--fa598e50bf7b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/istanbul-lion-hunt-ends-with-no-big-cat-found-after-all/a-80020913?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After a major search operation for a lion on the loose in Istanbul woodlands, Turkish authorities said "the animal was neither a lion nor any other big cat."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistani astronaut to join Chinese space mission</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef2636e8c2e3d69eca5ed74f0d59a570bfa66846154a838757e2f5a909697c85</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:07:59Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T09:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistani-astronaut-to-join-chinese-space-mission/a-80028922--3c985eac77fd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistani-astronaut-to-join-chinese-space-mission/a-80028922?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Pakistani astronaut is set to become to the first foreigner to board China's Tiangong space station. Muhammad Zeeshan Ali, a payload specialist, will join the Shenzhou-24 mission when it launches on Wednesday.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Chinese official gets death sentence in spy case, report says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93be140b88ece033844501d48f628f7f3ee5bd91e6d241449f2321aa28ac5544</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/chinese-official-gets-death-sentence-in-spy-case-report-says/a-80028393--388878bff1dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/chinese-official-gets-death-sentence-in-spy-case-report-says/a-80028393?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Chinese official recruited while working abroad was paid more than a million yuan to leak secrets, state-affiliated media reported.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>What happens if a nuclear weapon explodes in space?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0152b8b6319817fc03cb7ceb21263fbaea89e53998736c7719c5326177cb7c5a</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-happens-if-a-nuclear-weapon-explodes-in-space/a-80025827--a6201a0063e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-happens-if-a-nuclear-weapon-explodes-in-space/a-80025827?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Earth's atmosphere offers protection from a nuclear blast in space, but satellites are more exposed. We explain how radiation could damage them, why the effects can linger and what protection is possible.</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Volkswagen begins wage talks with IG Metall union</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:db61c9586e5fcaeb1274975ad9acd791f4b4a8eb918cc82c68f585466b980cce</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T08:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-begins-wage-talks-with-ig-metall-union/live-80028306--34d90226a697.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-volkswagen-begins-wage-talks-with-ig-metall-union/live-80028306?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's largest labor union IG Metall and automaker Volkswagen are holding wage negotiations, as the company looks to embark on cost-cutting measures. Meanwhile, Germany's president is in Ghana. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Exiled leader Sheikh Hasina plans to return to Bangladesh on Dec. 16</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:93704c83818fad4c45ef1033f41a5f89a4316b420d22457f696b9a006d3eee20</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T07:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/exiled-leader-sheikh-hasina-plans-to-return-to-bangladesh-on-dec-16/a-80028083--b9b8951e810c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/exiled-leader-sheikh-hasina-plans-to-return-to-bangladesh-on-dec-16/a-80028083?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two years of exile in India, ousted Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina has set a return date to Bangladesh. She was sentenced to death in absentia last year over a brutal crackdown that left hundreds dead.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Weapons, war and wavering trust: Germans want to see more restraint in foreign policy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:dc5a59fd34be39fe1f74f9c5aa5882a84e3209ac98fb9c8cc3d3505b3cb1398a</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T05:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254--66b3f174435c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/weapons-war-and-wavering-trust-germans-want-to-see-more-restraint-in-foreign-policy/a-80026254?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">According to a study by the Körber Foundation, a growing number of Germans now oppose providing military aid to Ukraine. The majority also believes that Germany should take a neutral position between the US and China.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>India: Report warns of deepening authoritarianism under Modi</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aa1f61a75e89523672dba5f5b52908a0c6fd1ea4098ee7e406a0afbc15c2b7f7</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-24T04:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-report-warns-of-deepening-authoritarianism-under-modi/live-80027405--62ea9ba89a08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-report-warns-of-deepening-authoritarianism-under-modi/live-80027405?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A Human Rights Watch report found that Modi's rule in India has eroded the rule of law and "systematically weakened institutions" meant to protect freedoms. Also, in Delhi a man injured nine police with a knife.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US adds Megaspeed, at center of Nvidia scandal, to a trade blacklist</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d77afe383d55e30ce573a45450e5605ff62ed75df1970b5dc6d90a2bfda9cec7</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:08:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T22:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-adds-megaspeed-at-center-of-nvidia-scandal-to-a-trade-blacklist/a-80026849--f5370c0bb019.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-adds-megaspeed-at-center-of-nvidia-scandal-to-a-trade-blacklist/a-80026849?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Trump administration has added Megaspeed to a trade blacklist after tensions over its failure to do so raised questions. The news came the same day that Jensen Huang was reinstated as Nvidia's CEO.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Denmark: Top court backs hardline immigration "ghetto law"</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6ddceb3e1959353dd6069318ae3f6b9005220e976dc7ea6f7b0d026c1b25fde1</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T20:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/denmark-top-court-backs-hardline-immigration-ghetto-law/a-80026478--7ebce97025f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/denmark-top-court-backs-hardline-immigration-ghetto-law/a-80026478?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Denmark's Supreme Court has found that evictions of "non-Western" residents do not amount to discrimination. The government in Copenhagen argues its "ghetto law" encourages integration.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tajikistan follows US call, withdraws from ICC</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b16abc08a32b9557e34eaf5a36a564077f4fb8290b3f21c7aaff62fba8580175</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T18:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tajikistan-follows-us-call-withdraws-from-icc/a-80023903--9937f6abaec0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tajikistan-follows-us-call-withdraws-from-icc/a-80023903?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Tajikistan has initiated its withdrawal from the International Criminal Court as the US calls for it to be "dismantled." The decision was made during a recent visit from Russian President Vladimir Putin.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US and UK to host Women's World Cups in 2031 and 2035</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:24fd8dc026bf9ca668e8171376e68e3abc26b7ba201f628c938ad5108fbaba2b</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786--81630f151694.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">FIFA has confirmed the United States, Mexico, Costa Rica and Jamaica will host the 2031 Women's World Cup — the first to feature 48 teams. The UK will stage the 2035 edition, its first World Cup since 1966.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>After Japan's APEC snub, what's next for its China ties?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:071e5f162e49634acf6f2a596f76e598003e1387ffac2147df10cb45545e60d2</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823--0940c063c8fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-japan-s-apec-snub-what-s-next-for-its-china-ties/a-80020823?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Japan has long-running concerns over Chinese military expansionism, and Beijing has bristled at Sanae Takaichi's comments on Taiwan. The frosty ties were on full display at the APEC summit.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7392fd1ad1eac7d30f29bf463780cc87fa1610860fe868c3a8ee95be0c72da13</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal's new PM eyes closer ties with India amid lingering disputes</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd6836fd6dcde7f2974dd509dacff384b30c6aee49ea5196ed0f1b101380ac53</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769--65c0c20879de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-s-new-pm-eyes-closer-ties-with-india-amid-lingering-disputes/a-80021769?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On his first foreign bilateral visit, rapper-turned-Prime Minister Balendra Shah sought deeper ties with Nepal's neighbor and largest trading partner, while steering clear of sticky territorial issues.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nvidia reinstates former CEO Jensen Huang despite China espionage scandal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a551c8c8477ff98c14ee3cf2dc5562ca1a8878a71341c32bfc859773b02af718</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926--88659c21678b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nvidia-reinstates-former-ceo-jensen-huang-despite-china-espionage-scandal/a-80021926?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nvidia's board voted unanimously to bring back the disgraced CEO, who resigned this month amid news of his affairs. He's suspected of having had a relationship with a Chinese intelligence asset.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>North Macedonia remains stalled on its EU path after 21 years as a candidate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fb6b36986cad1fa3e30568d42d4540f6ecf40124d57f6373ac99def4653f410a</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841--291e539f1390.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/north-macedonia-remains-stalled-on-its-eu-path-after-21-years-as-a-candidate/a-80020841?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">EU enlargement has regained momentum, with Montenegro and Albania moving closer to membership. But North Macedonia, a candidate since 2005, remains stalled by a politically difficult dispute involving Bulgaria.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda minister at COP31: 'We need a just transition'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb9993c034e44e712c6129dd6d867941f2b157aac989b0904efd5ca64c474ad4</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209--312e033bb073.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-minister-at-cop31-we-need-a-just-transition/a-79997209?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Funding from wealthy countries to help deal with the impacts of climate change hasn't materialized, says Uganda's environment minister. The East African country is hoping oil and carbon credits will help boost finances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>COP deadlock prompts calls for a reset of climate diplomacy</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55a258e133aa731bbc9f8d9e4c339a22b21830adfb2cbe691c4e35cf20bd5d28</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T13:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494--3b4f8cad49dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop-deadlock-prompts-calls-for-a-reset-of-climate-diplomacy/a-80020494?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">COP31 has been branded a failure after countries couldn't reach a final agreement, divided over a reference to "fossil fuels." But was the decision to walk away from a watered-down text actually a show of strength?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>German police respond to multiple school bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3b5fa0839157c494c551ccaff0f770cad261b7220bac349a69bc776a2724fda</id><updated>2026-11-24T10:06:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T11:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842--56ba1301d92a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-respond-to-multiple-school-bomb-threats/a-80018842?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police in Germany are responding to bomb threats against a series of schools, but say that at present they don't believe them to be credible. Danish authorities are reporting a similar series of apparent hoaxes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
